## Iteration 8 — 2026-04-16

Three items from iter-7's parked list shipped: the reactive-binding
factoring, auto-consensus synthesis, and the gpt-5 param fallback.
The synthesis step makes the cross-check loop genuinely automatic —
no more manual "which of these points did both models raise?"

### What shipped

* **``saga2d.util.reactive.ReactiveValue[T]``** — single abstraction
  for "slot that accepts either ``T`` or ``Callable[[], T]``", with
  ``refresh()`` / ``set()`` / ``is_reactive`` / optional ``on_change``
  callback. Six property tests cover static pass-through, callable
  refresh, change-detection return value, explicit-set unbinding,
  and on_change firing on both refresh and set.
* **Label + ProgressBar migrated** to use ``ReactiveValue``. Label's
  text now stores ``ReactiveValue[str]`` with an on_change callback
  that invalidates font cache and marks layout dirty. ProgressBar
  uses two ``ReactiveValue[float]`` slots (value + max_value).
  Widget-specific validation (NaN rejection on ProgressBar) stays
  at the widget; binding mechanics live in the helper. Zero
  regression — the 15 existing reactive + text_style tests pass
  unchanged.
* **Auto-consensus synthesis** (``ai_review.synthesise_consensus``).
  After ``cross_check()`` returns ≥2 critiques, a third, neutral
  model (Claude Haiku 4.5, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) reads both and emits
  a structured output::

      ## CONSENSUS
      - <issue>: <how both framed it>
      ## DRIFT (single-reviewer, noise)
      - Reviewer A only: <…>
      - Reviewer B only: <…>
      ## RECOMMENDED NEXT ACTION
      <one concrete change, ≤40 words>

  The v15 test run distinguished "typography + label-placement
  systematic inconsistency" (both flag → consensus) from "YOU-to-S
  collision" (Gemini only → drift) and "title dominates HUD"
  (OpenAI only → drift).
* **gpt-5.x ``max_completion_tokens`` fallback** — ``call_openai``
  now tries the modern field name first, catches the specific HTTP
  400 from older models, and retries with ``max_tokens``. gpt-5.1
  now succeeds silently where iter-7 fell back to gpt-4o with
  stderr noise.

178 tests pass (6 new for ReactiveValue; Label/ProgressBar existing
tests unchanged).

### Auto-consensus at work on v15

    ## CONSENSUS
    - Text placement inconsistency: labels positioned arbitrarily
      around nodes lack systematic positioning rules.
    - Typography needs standardization: multiple font sizes and
      alignments feel unstyled.
    - Node label positioning broken at scale: text around nodes
      isn't anchored systematically, will fail with localisation.

    ## DRIFT (noise)
    - Gemini only: YOU↔S outline collision; 'O' too abstract.
    - GPT-5.1 only: title dominates HUD; controls padding; floor
      text collision risk.

    ## RECOMMENDED NEXT ACTION
    Define and apply a consistent text positioning system: place all
    node labels at a fixed vertical offset below their circles,
    centred. Use a single font size for node text.

*Note the synthesis is pointing at work that would partially revert
iter-6's radial placement — the radial layout fixed a concrete
"``→ floor 2`` over E" collision but both models now read radial as
"chaotic." Real design tension; logged rather than acted on this
round, because the reactive + synthesis work is already a full
iteration.*

### Why the synthesis step matters

The iter-7 cross-check proved two models + human diff reveals
consensus. This round made the diff automatic. Time to signal
dropped from "read both critiques, mentally overlap, decide" to
"read the CONSENSUS list." For a 5-minute iteration this is
substantial; for a 50-iteration project it's the difference
between the loop staying on-target and drifting into polish-game.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **``ReactiveValue`` has a ``default`` kwarg** so callable-based
   sources have something to return before their first refresh.
   Awkward — the callable knows its own "initial" value. Could make
   ``default`` optional and call the callable once at construction
   to seed the snapshot. Not critical.
2. **Claude synthesiser is pay-to-play** (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). The
   sys returns ``None`` cleanly when absent, but the user loses
   the automation. A zero-dep fallback (naive string-diff of the
   two critiques) would degrade gracefully.
3. **Single recommended action comes from the synthesiser's own
   taste**. For v15 it recommended reverting radial placement —
   that might be the right call, but the synthesiser is an LLM
   itself and carries its own visual biases. The recommendation
   field is a *suggestion*, not a vote. Logged.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

One refactor (ReactiveValue helper), one methodology upgrade
(auto-consensus), one parameter-drift fix (gpt-5.x). The refactor
is maintenance debt paid off before iteration 9 needs a fourth
reactive widget.

### Parked for iteration 9

* **Address the consensus recommendation**: unify node-label
  positioning so both reviewers stop flagging "chaotic text."
  Candidate approach — fixed below-node placement, uniform offset,
  centred, and rephrase ``→ floor 2`` to ``floor 2`` (no arrow,
  no ``→`` character extending horizontally).
* **Bundle a game font** — persistent typography complaint; now
  listed in consensus, not just single-model drift.
* **``_lighten_color`` deduplication** — still 4 copies.
* **``ReactiveValue.default`` ergonomic simplification** — seed
  snapshot from one-shot callable invocation.
* **Graceful fallback when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY absent**: naive
  overlap extraction so the synthesis step still helps without a
  third-party key.

