## Iteration 12 — 2026-04-16

Two more parked items shipped as pure API wins. Visual verification
of the iter-10/11/12 stack is still blocked — ``pyglet.display``
returns empty ``screens`` from every subprocess this session, so
no render landed. The code correctness is covered by 590 tests.

### What shipped

* **``ReactiveValue`` default is now optional when source is callable**.
  Previously every widget wrote::

      ReactiveValue(source, default="")

  which was annoying because the callable could just be invoked once
  at construction to seed the snapshot. Now::

      ReactiveValue(lambda: f"HP {self.hp}")

  — the callable fires once at construction. Pass ``default=`` only
  when you want a specific initial value before the first
  :meth:`refresh` (e.g. deferring a side-effectful first read).
  Two new tests cover the seed-from-callable path and the
  explicit-default override.
* **``saga2d.ring_budget(viewport, count, ...)``** — pure-math helper
  returning ``(ring_r, node_r)`` that fits *count* labelled nodes in
  *viewport* without sub-labels crashing top/bottom margins. Closes
  the iter-9 friction ("iterating on ring-layout geometry is
  trial-and-error; no helper that says 'given a viewport and a node
  count, what's the max ring_r that keeps labels from colliding?'").
  Four property tests cover: non-negative radii, vertical-margin fit,
  per-node radius shrinks with node count, zero-return on impossibly
  small viewports.
* **Ring of Pain now uses ``ring_budget``** — the magic ``* 0.32``
  literal tuned over iterations 1–9 by hand is gone. The ring
  geometry is computed from the viewport plus the sub-label
  footprint and the title/HUD margins.

590 mock-backend tests pass.

### The magic-literal reduction

At iteration 9 the draw code was::

    ring_r = min(w, h - 120) * 0.32
    node_r = int(min(w, h - 120) * 0.09)

Three hand-tuned numbers (``120``, ``0.32``, ``0.09``) that had
drifted across nine rounds of cross-check feedback. After
iteration 12::

    ring_r, node_r_f = ring_budget(
        (w, h), self.ring_size,
        margin_top=60, margin_bottom=88, margin_x=40,
        label_height=14, label_gap=18,
    )

Every number is named and describes a concrete visual role (title
height, HUD height, label size). A different game tuning its ring
layout doesn't have to retune the same ``0.32`` from scratch — it
passes the margins its HUD actually needs.

### Meta: visual-verification backlog now three iterations deep

iter-10, iter-11, iter-12 all shipped without a pyglet render.
Every subprocess spawn returns ``screens == []`` deep in
pyglet-cocoa. Reproduces with venv python directly too — not a
``uv run`` / subprocess issue, it's the macOS session state.
Earlier iterations (v1–v17) worked; something changed outside the
repo. When pyglet recovers, the first action is a full
render + cross-check + synthesis on the combined iter-10..12
stack.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **``ring_budget`` still hard-codes "one label footprint above and
   below the ring"** because that fits the Ring-of-Pain pattern
   specifically. A more general helper would take a list of
   "fixture positions" (``top_node_label``, ``bottom_node_label``,
   etc.) and compute around each. Parked until a second game uses
   the helper and that generality becomes necessary.
2. **Every new util helper gets re-exported from both
   ``saga2d.util`` and ``saga2d``**. Cheap duplication; fine for
   now but a ``__getattr__`` shim on top-level ``saga2d`` would
   save the double-update pattern. Not urgent.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

``ReactiveValue`` seed-from-callable optional; ``ring_budget``
utility that replaces magic literals in Ring of Pain.

