— same ``IndexError: list index out of range`` deep in
pyglet-cocoa. macOS session state remains un-recovered. Logged.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **``Scene.controls`` mixing tuple and string keys in the same
   dict is correct but reads awkwardly**::

       controls = {
           ("right", "d"):        "rotate_cw",
           ("left", "a"):         "rotate_ccw",
           ("confirm", "space"):  "confirm",
           "cancel":              "cancel",        # single-key odd one out
       }

   A ``("cancel",)`` tuple-of-one might normalise the rule
   ("keys are always tuples") at the cost of a slightly uglier
   call site. Current behaviour is fine but noted.
2. **``Anchor.TOP`` / ``BOTTOM`` / ``CENTER`` don't have
   ``TOP_CENTER`` / ``BOTTOM_CENTER`` aliases** — both common HUD
   positions. Fine for now; readers have to remember ``Anchor.TOP``
   centers horizontally already.
3. **No built-in "option selector" pattern** — every game with a
   choice menu writes the same "current index mod N" logic. A tiny
   ``Selector`` state helper (wraps/clamps/emits events) would
   reduce dial-menu's 4 lines of ``(self.selected + 1) % N`` to
   zero. Flagged for when a third game needs it.

