* **``examples/tictactoe/``** — the third saga2d example, 144 lines
  including full win detection, draw detection, reset, and status
  bar. Deliberately non-radial:
    - ``grid_positions(9, columns=3, ...)`` for the 3x3 board —
      *not* ``ring_positions``. This is the first example that uses
      ``grid_positions``.
    - Cursor navigation via ``Scene.controls`` with 6 aliases
      (arrows + WASD + space + R for reset).
    - Reactive ``Label(self._status_text, text_style="heading")``
      — passes a method as the callable source directly, letting
      the status text (``"X's turn"`` / ``"O wins!"`` / ``"Draw!"``)
      fall out of game state each frame.
    - ``Anchor.TOP_CENTER`` / ``BOTTOM_CENTER`` / ``BOTTOM_LEFT``
      — the iter-14 aliases finally get used.
