### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **Tic-tac-toe's cell-border rendering uses two ``draw_rect``
   calls per cell** (outer line + inner fill). saga2d has no
   "draw a filled rectangle *with a border*" primitive; you
   compose from two solid fills. Works, but the three lines per
   cell add up. A ``draw_rect(..., border_color=…, border_width=…)``
   kwarg would halve the draw call count and read cleaner. Parked.
2. **``grid_positions`` returns cell centres, but grid rendering
   usually wants cell corners** too (for the border). Either the
   helper returns both, or the game computes corners from centres
   and cell size (what tic-tac-toe does). Fine; noted.
3. **The ``Anchor.TOP_CENTER`` vs ``TOP`` equivalence isn't
   discoverable from autocomplete** — both exist, both are the
   same instance. Sphinx docs would enumerate them; nothing in
   the type system surfaces "these are aliases." Flagged for
   when saga2d has proper API docs.

