  ReactiveValue helper, Anchor aliases, lighten)
* Four declarative API patterns (controls, reactive HUD,
  Row/Column, theme text_styles)

…all without a single rendered pixel. The mock-only discipline
was a forcing function that steered iterations toward API quality
over polish. The stack this produced is probably tighter than one
steered by visual-polish demands would have been.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **Tutorial snippets that build on each other need careful
   variable-name discipline**. Each step's snippet should be
   self-contained (paste + run), but that means re-declaring the
   full class every time. Total tutorial is ~140 lines of code
   across 5 snippets because of this repetition. Could be solved
   with a `"# ...continuing from step N"` convention; not worth
   it for a 5-step tutorial.
2. **Markdown + verified-snippet pair is a good pattern**. The
   README (iter-18) did this with one snippet; the tutorial
   (iter-21) does it with five. If saga2d grows more docs, a
   shared ``tests/examples/_snippet_harness.py`` helper would
   cut the boilerplate — each test is a ``class`` + a few
   ``game.tick()`` calls.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

One tutorial (``tutorials/declarative/tutorial.md``), 10 snippet
tests, a README link. The longest-outstanding non-rendering
parked item is closed.

